.SH NAME
SDL_EnterAppMainCallbacks \- An entry point for SDL\(aqs use in
.BR SDL_MAIN_USE_CALLBACKS .

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_main.h>
.PP
.BI "int SDL_EnterAppMainCallbacks(int argc, char *argv[], SDL_AppInit_func appinit, SDL_AppIterate_func appiter, SDL_AppEvent_func appevent, SDL_AppQuit_func appquit);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generally, you should not call this function directly\[char46] This only exists to hand off work into SDL as soon as possible, where it has a lot more control and functionality available, and make the inline code in
.BR SDL_main \[char46]h
as small as possible\[char46]
.PP
Not all platforms use this, it\(aqs actual use is hidden in a magic header-only library, and you should not call this directly unless you _really_ know what you\(aqre doing\[char46]

